# Written for this pack by BurN-30 (GPL-3.0). Replaces 12-dalaran.guide (adapted from Aurum's chapter
# aurum-druid/dalaran-finale, Aurums Night Elf Druid Guide 0.4.37, GPL-3.0) on Polestar's own route,
# rebuilt from the Image of Archmage Modera's camp. Sources: Polestar 0.4.2.2 (GPL-3.0), its `when
# dungeon "City of Dalaran"` steps of forever/alliance/30-40/05-arathi-highlands (Modera's camp on
# the lake shore west of Dalaran, just over the Silverpine border; the sewer grate in the western wall
# 30 yards away, at Alterac Mountains 8.8,59.5 from players' recordings; Heart of Disruption brings
# the Dalaran Sewer Key), data/dungeon-runs.json and its Dungeons codex (quests, objectives, bosses);
# the way through the city and the bosses from Warcraft Tavern's City of Dalaran guide (read
# 23/11/2026), rewritten. Not played in game yet.
#
# Self-contained chapter for Polestar's route: the Groupe Alliance module offers it once An Alarming
# Request (92432, level 30) is taken from Emissary Jacques in Southshore
# (forever/alliance/30-40/01-hillsbrad-foothills, about 31), or handed in to Modera
# (30-40/05-arathi-highlands, about 37) for whoever put it off. From Southshore it is a short ride to
# Modera; the run follows at once and the hand-ins are in the same camp.
# Since 0.13.0 the chapter has the id its guide had up to 0.12.x (groupe-alliance/12-dalaran): a tab saved on it opens
# the chapter.
#
# Compared with Polestar's run (at about 37, Modera's two quests, no bosses): the same camp, grate
# and quests, offered from 31 when the dungeon (28 to 35, codex floor 31.7) still gives its full XP,
# with the bosses one by one and the order through the city. The old chapter's Stormwind start is
# gone: A Green Sample and Power Overwhelming (92456, 92489) are offered in Stormwind by the Gnomeregan
# chapter (about 31) and done here for whoever holds them; their hand-ins wait for the route's next
# Stormwind stop, where Polestar lists them. The end of the Defias story (393 to 396) moved to the
# Stockade chapter. Left out, as by Polestar: Friend of the Kirin Tor (92459, 270 XP for a walk),
# Unstable Magic (96603, level 60).
guide groupe-alliance/12-dalaran
title Dungeon · City of Dalaran (30-38)
folder Group Alliance
category Dungeons
faction Alliance
levels 30-38
zone Alterac Mountains

step Southshore: Emissary Jacques
  zone Hillsbrad Foothills
  tip City of Dalaran: a 5-player Forever dungeon in the Alterac Mountains, levels 28 to 35 in the group finder. Emissary Jacques's errand leads to the Image of Archmage Modera, by the city's wall: she gives the dungeon's two quests and the key of its sewers. His quest needs level 30.
  note Keep 4 free quest log slots.
  accept 92432                                -- Emissary Jacques

step Image of Archmage Modera
  zone Silverpine Forest
  tip North-west past Hillsbrad Fields and round Dalaran's dome, keeping clear of Tarren Mill: the Kirin Tor camp is on the lake shore west of the city, just over the border into Silverpine Forest.
  turnin 92432                                -- Image of Archmage Modera
  accept 92457                                -- Starving Arcane
  accept 92458                                -- Heart of Disruption: it brings the Dalaran Sewer Key

step Stormwind's two quests, for whoever took them
  when onquest 92456,92489
  zone Stormwind City
  tip A Green Sample (Shylamiir) and Power Overwhelming (High Sorcerer Andromath), offered in Stormwind by the Gnomeregan chapter: both are done inside.
  accept 92456 optional                       -- Shylamiir, Stormwind
  accept 92489 optional                       -- High Sorcerer Andromath, Stormwind

step City of Dalaran: the sewer grate
  zone Alterac Mountains
  tip The way in is the sewer grate in the city's western wall, by the lake, 30 yards from Modera's camp: the key opens it for the group.
  note In the log before going in: Starving Arcane and Heart of Disruption (Modera); A Green Sample and Power Overwhelming for whoever took them in Stormwind. Share each quest with the group: click it in the quest log, then Share.
  goto 8.8,59.5 "City of Dalaran" r 20

step The sewers: Atrexis the Grave Knight
  tip Inside the Cantrips & Crows, cross the bridge and turn right: three large pipes lead to the Underbelly. Mindless Horrors fear (a Shaman's Tremor Totem helps), Kirin Tor Necromancers raise skeletons two at a time: the tank picks them up. Atrexis, in the summoning circle, is a stronger necromancer: clear the undead around him without pulling him, then a Shaman can purge his Unholy Frenzy.
  note The square room by the sewers' exit holds a summoning circle: only with a Tome of Dalaran (from Shadowfang Keep, a Horde dungeon) does it call the hidden boss, Lyn the Ignored.
  kill 247126                                 -- Atrexis the Grave Knight

step The streets of Dalaran: along the way
  along until dal-shade
  tip Out of the sewers, the arcane remnants are all over the streets: Seeking and Saturated Remnants for Modera. A Saturated Remnant leaves a Mana Leak field when it dies (casters stand in it), Mana Fiends explode when they die (spread out), Mana Phantoms cast Mana Burn (interrupt it).
  kill 247003 quest 92457.1                   -- Seeking Remnant
  kill 247001 quest 92457.2                   -- Saturated Remnant

step The Violet Hold: Mana Devourer
  tip Left from the sewers' exit. Clear every enemy of the hold first: they join the fight. The mana serpent drains the tank and hits the whole group now and then: heal through it.
  kill 246008                                 -- Mana Devourer

step Krasus' Landing: Arcane Anomaly
  tip Back out and right. Clear the landing, then everyone stands close behind the boss: its Focal Blast is a beam that turns round it, easy to walk round from up close.
  kill 245999                                 -- Arcane Anomaly

step Runeweaver Square: Fel Ancient
  tip Into the middle of the city from the east: Magus Fansy Goodbringer, by the magic shield, lowers it. The Fel Ancient roots two players and drops burning fel timber under them: a Druid's shapeshift or a Paladin's Blessing of Freedom frees them. The Fel Infused Blossom for A Green Sample is one of the big green bulbs of the square.
  kill 246003                                 -- Fel Ancient
  collect 251983 quest 92456 optional         -- Fel Infused Blossom: a green bulb of the square

step Path of Renewal: Arcanic Enigma
  tip Counter-clockwise to the north-east, by Antonidas's statue. Kill its two Mana Phantoms first. The Enigma polymorphs players and silences everyone close to it: ranged players keep away.
  kill 246016 quest 92489 optional            -- Arcanic Enigma

step Magus Commerce Exchange: Unstable Sentry
  tip West through the city, in a nook of the market. Spread out; when it casts Malfunction, everyone but the tank steps well away.
  kill 246017                                 -- Unstable Sentry

step The Violet Citadel: Shade of the Archmage
  label dal-shade
  tip Archmage Modera waits on the citadel's steps: talk to her for the portal to the Violet Chamber. A small room: ranged players spread out. Step out of the way of the slow bouncing orb (Bounding Mana). Out of mana, he polymorphs the whole group and casts Evocation: whoever can break free hits him then. Each player on Heart of Disruption loots the Arcane Mote.
  kill 246020                                 -- Shade of the Archmage
  collect 251961 quest 92458                  -- Arcane Mote

step Modera's rewards
  zone Silverpine Forest
  tip Back out through the grate to Modera's camp. Last stop of the chapter: the route's own guide comes back once these are handed in. A Green Sample and Power Overwhelming go to Stormwind: Polestar lists them at the route's next Stormwind stop.
  turnin 92457                                -- Image of Archmage Modera
  turnin 92458                                -- Image of Archmage Modera
